Pat ran just check in dotfiles/notmuch on beastie, where mbsync and
msmtp are not installed yet. Every check failed, and nothing said
why, since the check hides each command's output.

Patch 1 makes just check report mbsync, msmtp, and notmuch first. If
any is missing, it prints the pkg install line that provides it and
stops, so the other checks do not pile up failures for the same
cause. Patch 2 documents how beastie gets the mail ports: they are in
its ports list, so a boot environment built from it has them, and
until beastie runs one, "doas pkg install isync msmtp notmuch"
installs them on the running system.

The series goes on top of "[PATCH v2 00/16] Move beastie and
lab-claude onto lab-mail" [1], as Pat asked in "Re: [PATCH v2 06/16]
dotfiles/notmuch: Add a check of the lab-mail client" [2]. Its
patches are the prerequisite-patch-id lines below.

Tested on lab-claude: with a PATH that lacks mbsync and msmtp, just
check prints a FAIL line for each, the line "pkg install isync
msmtp", and exits 1 before any other check. With all three present,
it prints three ok lines and runs the checks as before.

